      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.63,
          "end": 2.46,
          "en": "So how can we provide",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 2.46,
          "end": 6.12,
          "en": "the task status options here now?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.12,
          "end": 11.12,
          "en": "Well, we could do that in the main TS file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 11.19,
          "end": 13.413,
          "en": "by adding it to the provider's array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 14.34,
          "end": 15.6,
          "en": "If you would do that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.6,
          "end": 18.75,
          "en": "then the value would be injectable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.75,
          "end": 20.703,
          "en": "in the entire application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 22.2,
          "end": 26.13,
          "en": "But actually, I only need it in the tasks-list component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 26.13,
          "end": 28.89,
          "en": "and the task-item component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 28.89,
          "end": 31.53,
          "en": "which is actually a child component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 31.53,
          "end": 34.98,
          "en": "of the tasks list component and therefore,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 34.98,
          "end": 38.853,
          "en": "providing it there would be enough in this application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 39.93,
          "end": 41.82,
          "en": "so we could do that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 41.82,
          "end": 45.21,
          "en": "We can go to the tasks list component, TypeScript file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 45.21,
          "end": 47.92,
          "en": "and there to the component decorator object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 48.9,
          "end": 51.303,
          "en": "and add this providers array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 52.53,
          "end": 54.87,
          "en": "And then here I wanna add a provider",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 54.87,
          "end": 57.13,
          "en": "which uses a custom injection token",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 58.05,
          "end": 61.08,
          "en": "and therefore, I'll go to the task model ts file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 61.08,
          "end": 64.32,
          "en": "and also export an injection token here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 64.32,
          "end": 65.76,
          "en": "We don't have to do it here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 65.76,
          "end": 68.07,
          "en": "but I guess it makes sense to keep it close",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 68.07,
          "end": 70.203,
          "en": "to the value that will be injected.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 71.37,
          "end": 74.58,
          "en": "And I'll name my token here, TASK STATUS OPTIONS,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 74.58,
          "end": 77.07,
          "en": "written like this because that's also",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 77.07,
          "end": 79.89,
          "en": "a common notation you'll often see",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 79.89,
          "end": 81.84,
          "en": "for injection tokens",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 81.84,
          "end": 86.133,
          "en": "that this all-caps notation here is being used.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 87.39,
          "end": 89.07,
          "en": "But ultimately, it's up to you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 89.07,
          "end": 92.43299999999999,
          "en": "which name you wanna use for your injection token.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 93.42,
          "end": 96.53999999999999,
          "en": "But here, I'll then import injection token",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 96.53999999999999,
          "end": 100.35300000000001,
          "en": "from @angular core and construct a new one like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 101.85,
          "end": 106.65,
          "en": "And then also add this description, task status options.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 106.65,
          "end": 109.77000000000001,
          "en": "And I wanna let TypeScript know which kind of data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 109.77000000000001,
          "end": 113.4,
          "en": "will be provided through that injection token.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 113.4,
          "end": 114.45,
          "en": "And that, of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 114.45,
          "end": 117.72,
          "en": "will be this task status options thing here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 117.72,
          "end": 120.39,
          "en": "which has this type signature.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 120.39,
          "end": 123.63,
          "en": "Therefore, I'll actually grab this type definition,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 123.63,
          "end": 127.08,
          "en": "cut it, and set it up as a separate custom type,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 127.08,
          "end": 129.54,
          "en": "so that we can easily reuse it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 129.54,
          "end": 134.54,
          "en": "and name this TaskStatusOptions, like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 136.77,
          "end": 140.433,
          "en": "Assign that as a type here and use it here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 144.32999999999998,
          "end": 147,
          "en": "With that, it's clear that this injection token here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 147,
          "end": 151.2,
          "en": "will be used to provide a value of this shape,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 151.2,
          "end": 154.413,
          "en": "an array full of objects with this shape here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 156.3,
          "end": 157.98,
          "en": "In the tasks list component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 157.98,
          "end": 159.24,
          "en": "we can, therefore, now use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 159.24,
          "end": 163.47,
          "en": "this task status options token here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 163.47,
          "end": 165.903,
          "en": "after importing it from task model.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 167.37,
          "end": 170.79,
          "en": "By the way, this service import isn't needed here anymore,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 170.79,
          "end": 172.083,
          "en": "but this token is,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 173.13,
          "end": 177.12,
          "en": "and then we have to use one of these use properties.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 177.12,
          "end": 179.79,
          "en": "And now, it's not a class I wanna provide,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 179.79,
          "end": 184.53,
          "en": "but instead a value which we can do with use value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 184.53,
          "end": 188.67,
          "en": "because it's a simple constant array which I wanna provide,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 188.67,
          "end": 190.89,
          "en": "which is a simple value in the end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 190.89,
          "end": 194.31,
          "en": "It's not a class that needs to be instantiated first,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 194.31,
          "end": 197.64,
          "en": "instead it's an existing value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 197.64,
          "end": 201.21,
          "en": "An alternative would be to use factory",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 201.21,
          "end": 202.89,
          "en": "that would take a function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 202.89,
          "end": 207.12,
          "en": "which is then executed in case you had some value that needs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 207.12,
          "end": 210.32999999999998,
          "en": "to be generated dynamically which could be the case",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 210.32999999999998,
          "end": 212.34300000000002,
          "en": "for more complex values,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 213.32999999999998,
          "end": 216.54,
          "en": "but here, it's really just use value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 216.54,
          "end": 220.65,
          "en": "And then it's this task status options value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 220.65,
          "end": 223.413,
          "en": "this constant which is imported from task model.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 224.97,
          "end": 227.13,
          "en": "Therefore, what I'll actually do here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 227.13,
          "end": 230.4,
          "en": "is I'll cut this provider object definition",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 230.4,
          "end": 235.09,
          "en": "from my tasks list component and remove these imports",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 236.19,
          "end": 240.7,
          "en": "and instead go to the task model file and set that up here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 241.89,
          "end": 244.68,
          "en": "because I have the value and the token here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 244.68,
          "end": 247.77,
          "en": "Why not also define the provider here?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 247.77,
          "end": 250.62,
          "en": "So I'll export a constant named taskStatusOptionsProvider",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 253.98,
          "end": 257.4,
          "en": "which will store this provider configuration",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 257.4,
          "end": 259.98,
          "en": "and which should be of type provider,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 259.98,
          "end": 263.943,
          "en": "which is a type that's imported from @angular core.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 266.55,
          "end": 269.82,
          "en": "You don't need to add that here, but by doing so,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 269.82,
          "end": 272.82,
          "en": "you make sure that you have a correct definition here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 272.82,
          "end": 275.373,
          "en": "and you don't have a typo in here, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 276.33,
          "end": 279.363,
          "en": "So that's why I am explicitly setting that type.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 280.47,
          "end": 283.56,
          "en": "And with that back in the tasks list component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 283.56,
          "end": 286.12,
          "en": "it's now simply that taskStatusOptionsProvider",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 287.67,
          "end": 290.13,
          "en": "which I'll import and add here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 290.13,
          "end": 292.203,
          "en": "which keeps the code here a bit leaner.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 294.3,
          "end": 296.22,
          "en": "Well, and with that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 296.22,
          "end": 300.69,
          "en": "finally this provider is set up",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 300.69,
          "end": 304.68,
          "en": "and registered with the element injector of this component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 304.68,
          "end": 306.87,
          "en": "So it's available in this component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 306.87,
          "end": 308.58,
          "en": "and all child components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 308.58,
          "end": 310.743,
          "en": "and we can, therefore, now inject it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 312.33,
          "end": 315.58,
          "en": "For example here, by adding a new property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 317.07,
          "end": 318.953,
          "en": "which we could name taskStatusOptions,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 320.066,
          "end": 323.19,
          "en": "the name is up to you though, which holds a value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 323.19,
          "end": 325.53,
          "en": "which we get with help of the inject function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 325.53,
          "end": 327.39,
          "en": "or with help of the constructor.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 327.39,
          "end": 330.243,
          "en": "You could also inject it there as you learned.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 331.26,
          "end": 333.63,
          "en": "But it's easier with the inject function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 333.63,
          "end": 336.93,
          "en": "because here we now just need our token,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 336.93,
          "end": 340.17,
          "en": "TASK STATUS OPTIONS, written like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 340.17,
          "end": 344.43,
          "en": "and of course, imported from the task model file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 344.43,
          "end": 345.603,
          "en": "And that's all.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 347.1,
          "end": 350.88,
          "en": "This adds this task status options property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 350.88,
          "end": 354.513,
          "en": "which we can now use to access the injected value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 355.77,
          "end": 359.85,
          "en": "And therefore, in the task list component HTML file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 359.85,
          "end": 364.17,
          "en": "we can now generate some of these options here dynamically.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 364.17,
          "end": 365.79,
          "en": "We can remove them here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 365.79,
          "end": 370.11,
          "en": "and use @for to loop through all the options",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 370.11,
          "end": 374.76,
          "en": "of our task status options",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 374.76,
          "end": 378.87,
          "en": "and track the option value, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 378.87,
          "end": 380.403,
          "en": "as a unique identifier,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 381.42,
          "end": 383.61,
          "en": "and then output one option element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 383.61,
          "end": 386.673,
          "en": "for every option in that injected array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 388.08,
          "end": 391.62,
          "en": "So it's then the option text that's output here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 391.62,
          "end": 396.62,
          "en": "for the value, it should be the option value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 396.69,
          "end": 398.61,
          "en": "and that's now a dynamic value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 398.61,
          "end": 401.46,
          "en": "So we need the property binding syntax here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 401.46,
          "end": 405,
          "en": "to bind the value property of this option",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 405,
          "end": 407.37,
          "en": "to the dynamically resolved value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 407.37,
          "end": 409.83299999999997,
          "en": "from the option object here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 412.29,
          "end": 414.03,
          "en": "And if we do all that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 414.03,
          "end": 417.81,
          "en": "and we save that all, if you go back to the application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 417.81,
          "end": 422.16,
          "en": "you see that you have still the same options as before here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 422.16,
          "end": 424.18,
          "en": "And we can also check whether they work",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 429.27,
          "end": 431.463,
          "en": "by changing the filter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 432.39,
          "end": 434.43,
          "en": "And that looks good to me.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 434.43,
          "end": 436.29,
          "en": "So we got the same options as",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 436.29,
          "end": 440.19,
          "en": "before here in that filter dropdown,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 440.19,
          "end": 443.82,
          "en": "but now they are generated dynamically",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 443.82,
          "end": 448.26,
          "en": "based on this injected value, which is now not a service,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 448.26,
          "end": 451.11,
          "en": "but instead some other value which we injected",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 451.11,
          "end": 453.93,
          "en": "with help of a custom injection token.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 453.93,
          "end": 455.88,
          "en": "And now, we can of course, also inject",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 455.88,
          "end": 459.153,
          "en": "that same value into the task item component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 135,
          "start": 460.40999999999997,
          "end": 464.97,
          "en": "Since that is a child component of the tasks list component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 136,
          "start": 464.97,
          "end": 467.58,
          "en": "it will have access to the element injector",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 137,
          "start": 467.58,
          "end": 470.4,
          "en": "of the tasks list component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 138,
          "start": 470.4,
          "end": 474.36,
          "en": "and it will be able to inject the task status options.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 139,
          "start": 474.36,
          "end": 477.81,
          "en": "So in the task item component TypeScript file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 140,
          "start": 477.81,
          "end": 481.27,
          "en": "we can add our taskStatusOptions as well",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 141,
          "start": 482.52,
          "end": 484.74,
          "en": "and inject them by using",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 142,
          "start": 484.74,
          "end": 487.653,
          "en": "the TASK STATUS OPTIONS injection token,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 143,
          "start": 488.61,
          "end": 491.8,
          "en": "which of course, also must be imported here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 144,
          "start": 492.72,
          "end": 495.42,
          "en": "and the service import isn't needed here anymore.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 145,
          "start": 495.42,
          "end": 498.543,
          "en": "We can remove that, but this token must be injected.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 146,
          "start": 499.74,
          "end": 504.74,
          "en": "And with it injected, we can go to the template here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 147,
          "start": 505.98,
          "end": 509.58,
          "en": "and now render these options dynamically.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 148,
          "start": 509.58,
          "end": 512.67,
          "en": "So again, we can use @for to go through",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 149,
          "start": 512.67,
          "end": 515.35,
          "en": "the options of task status options",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 150,
          "start": 517.08,
          "end": 521.04,
          "en": "and track the option value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 151,
          "start": 521.04,
          "end": 525.93,
          "en": "And then for every option in the task status options array,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 152,
          "start": 525.93,
          "end": 527.8,
          "en": "I wanna output an option element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 153,
          "start": 529.02,
          "end": 533.73,
          "en": "where the value is bound dynamically to option.value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 154,
          "start": 535.56,
          "end": 538.41,
          "en": "where selected is bound dynamically",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 155,
          "start": 538.41,
          "end": 543.41,
          "en": "to task status being equal to option.taskStatus",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 156,
          "start": 544.62,
          "end": 547.623,
          "en": "which is open in progress or done.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 157,
          "start": 549.33,
          "end": 554.33,
          "en": "And where the text here is set to option.text, like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 158,
          "start": 555.93,
          "end": 559.02,
          "en": "That's the code I wanna have here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 159,
          "start": 559.02,
          "end": 561.99,
          "en": "With that, we can get rid of these hard-coded options,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 160,
          "start": 561.99,
          "end": 564.09,
          "en": "and we now render this dropdown",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 161,
          "start": 564.09,
          "end": 566.61,
          "en": "with all its options dynamically,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 162,
          "start": 566.61,
          "end": 569.553,
          "en": "again, based on that injected value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 163,
          "start": 570.51,
          "end": 573.91,
          "en": "With that, again, if we add some tasks here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 164,
          "start": 575.19,
          "end": 578.97,
          "en": "like this, this dropdown works,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 165,
          "start": 578.97,
          "end": 581.58,
          "en": "changing the status also works,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 166,
          "start": 581.58,
          "end": 585.903,
          "en": "and filtering based on that status also works just fine,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 167,
          "start": 586.83,
          "end": 590.34,
          "en": "all without any errors here in the console",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 168,
          "start": 590.34,
          "end": 594.18,
          "en": "or here where the development server is running.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 169,
          "start": 594.18,
          "end": 597.75,
          "en": "And that's, therefore, an example for a custom provider",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 170,
          "start": 597.75,
          "end": 601.05,
          "en": "that provides a non-service,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 171,
          "start": 601.05,
          "end": 605.04,
          "en": "a non-class value, instead, a provider",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 172,
          "start": 605.04,
          "end": 607.29,
          "en": "that provides a regular array,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 173,
          "start": 607.29,
          "end": 611.64,
          "en": "which can then be injected into all interested components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 174,
          "start": 611.64,
          "end": 616.02,
          "en": "Here, I do register that provider with the element injector,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 175,
